# Dataset builder credentials (run commands from rules/dataset/).
#
# 1. Copy this reference once: cp -n env-config .env
# 2. Edit .env and paste your tokens after the equals signs below.
# 3. Load them when running authenticated commands:
#      uv run --no-sync --env-file .env magika-datasets hydrate --download --workers 8 --output .local/my-corpus
# Install dependencies first as described in README.md.
#
# .env is gitignored. This visible, versioned reference must keep empty values.
# Existing environment variables take precedence over values loaded from .env.

# VirusTotal:
# - Sign in at https://www.virustotal.com/ and open your user menu > API key.
# - Copy the key to VT_API_KEY in .env.
# - Intelligence search and file downloads require the corresponding premium
#   account privileges. A free API key alone does not enable this workflow.
# - Requests consume your account quota; begin with a small --limit.
# Docs: https://docs.virustotal.com/reference/authentication
#       https://docs.virustotal.com/reference/intelligence-search
#       https://docs.virustotal.com/reference/files-download-url
VT_API_KEY=

# GitHub (optional; increases API quota for issue discovery):
# - Open https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
# - Name the fine-grained token "dataset-builder" and choose an expiration.
# - Select public repository access; no additional permissions are needed for
#   the builder's public reads. Do not grant write or administration access.
# - Generate the token and copy it to GITHUB_TOKEN in .env.
# Public Git repository downloads work without this token.
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/authentication/keeping-your-account-and-data-secure/managing-your-personal-access-tokens
GITHUB_TOKEN=
